values ('ap_biology', 2, '2.3', array['2.3']::text[], 'convention', 'Orientation of embedded protein regions', 'Hydrophilic protein regions are inside the protein or exposed to the cytosol, and hydrophobic regions form the protein surface that interacts with the fatty acids in the membrane interior.', '[]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-biology-reference-u1-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_biology-u2-r1-023; ced=2.3.A.2.i-ii "Hydrophobic regions of proteins make up the protein surface that interacts with the fatty acids"')
