values ('ap_biology', 2, '2.4', array['2.4', '2.6']::text[], 'list_sequence', 'What crosses the membrane and how', 'Membrane passage depends on molecule size, polarity, and charge.', '[{"label": "Small nonpolar molecules (N2, O2, CO2)", "meaning": "Freely pass across the membrane"}, {"label": "Small polar, uncharged molecules (H2O, NH3)", "meaning": "Pass through in small amounts"}, {"label": "Large polar molecules and ions", "meaning": "Move through embedded channels and transport proteins"}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Nonpolar hydrocarbon tails prevent ions and polar molecules from crossing on their own, so cite the hydrophobic interior in an explanation.', 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-biology-reference-u1-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_biology-u2-r1-027; ced=2.4.A.2-3 "Small nonpolar molecules, including N2, O2, and CO2, freely pass across the membrane"')
