values ('ap_biology', 2, '2.6', array['2.6', '2.8']::text[], 'convention', 'Ions need channel proteins; ion movement can polarize membranes', 'Charged ions such as Na+ and K+ require channel proteins to cross the membrane, and the movement of ions across the membrane can polarize the membrane.', '[]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-biology-reference-u1-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_biology-u2-r2-008; ced=EK 2.6.A.1.i-ii: "Membranes may become polarized by the movement of ions across the membrane"; "Charged ions, including Na+ (sodium) and K+ (potassium), require channel proteins"')
